\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Information boundaries of budgeted score prediction. Historical scores support global factor fitting and cross-fitted donor calibration. A held-out model supplies only queried scores; these condition its latent representation and local donor weights. Sealed evaluation targets are never passed to the predictor. Query indices depend on fitted factors and earlier indices, not on the revealed score values. The diagram describes the evaluated computation, not evidence of a component-specific benefit.}}{2}{figure.caption.1}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:overview}{{1}{2}{Information boundaries of budgeted score prediction. Historical scores support global factor fitting and cross-fitted donor calibration. A held-out model supplies only queried scores; these condition its latent representation and local donor weights. Sealed evaluation targets are never passed to the predictor. Query indices depend on fitted factors and earlier indices, not on the revealed score values. The diagram describes the evaluated computation, not evidence of a component-specific benefit}{figure.caption.1}{}}
