\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Fixed-target MAE versus acquisition budget for model holdout (a) and heuristic-family holdout (b). Points average seeds; bars are descriptive sample standard deviations across the three seeds, not confidence intervals. Both panels share axes and retain the same targets across budgets. Simple references appear in Table~\ref {tab:main}; complete budget values are in the supplement.}}{7}{figure.caption.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:budget}{{2}{7}{Fixed-target MAE versus acquisition budget for model holdout (a) and heuristic-family holdout (b). Points average seeds; bars are descriptive sample standard deviations across the three seeds, not confidence intervals. Both panels share axes and retain the same targets across budgets. Simple references appear in Table~\ref {tab:main}; complete budget values are in the supplement}{figure.caption.6}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Matched model-holdout controls, averaged over budgets and seeds; bars show descriptive seed standard deviations. Constant history replaces each observed value by its historical column mean. Column-shifted history independently cyclically shifts each column's value/mask pairs. Small horizontal offsets separate overlapping points. The studied package does not beat column means after shifting; these conditions are not residual-only ablations.}}{7}{figure.caption.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:controls}{{3}{7}{Matched model-holdout controls, averaged over budgets and seeds; bars show descriptive seed standard deviations. Constant history replaces each observed value by its historical column mean. Column-shifted history independently cyclically shifts each column's value/mask pairs. Small horizontal offsets separate overlapping points. The studied package does not beat column means after shifting; these conditions are not residual-only ablations}{figure.caption.7}{}}
